      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>A.</alert>
The series <m>2 + 2 (0.2) + 2 (0.2)^2 + \cdots + 2 (0.2)^{11}</m>
has 12 terms, and its sum is
<me>2 + 2 (0.2) + 2 (0.2)^2 + \cdots + 2 (0.2)^{11} =
   {2 (1 - 0.2^{12})\over 1 - 0.2}.</me>




<alert>B.</alert>
The series 
<m>2 (0.2)^{5} + 2 (0.2)^{6} + 2 (0.2)^{7} + \cdots + 2 (0.2)^{12}</m>
has <m>12 - 5 + 1 = 8</m> terms.  We can write it as 
<me>2 (0.2)^{5} + 2 (0.2)^{6} + 2 (0.2)^{7} + \cdots + 
    2 (0.2)^{12} = (2 (0.2)^{5}) (1 + 0.2 + \cdots + 0.2^{7}),</me>
so its sum is 
<me>(2 (0.2)^{5}) (1 + 0.2 + \cdots + 0.2^{7}) = 
    {2 (0.2)^{5} (1 - 0.2^{8})\over 1 - 0.2}.</me>



</solution>
